<!-- The Quick Settings tile's icon: Material Symbols' filled rocket_launch (Google, Apache-2.0) —
     the same icon set the app's own icon variants (icons/variants/bolt|flash|electric|boost.svg)
     come from.

     Why not the app's own mark here: at tile size — 24dp in the shade — that mark is a filled
     rounded square with small cut-outs and reads as a blank plate (owner, looking at the tile
     picker: "Это очень плохо видно иконку notapp"). A tile is 24dp of one flat colour, so it gets
     a glyph that stays unmistakable at that size, and a rocket says what the app does: launch
     something, instantly.

     The path is in Material Symbols' own 960-unit space, whose y axis runs from -960 (top) to 0
     (bottom); an Android viewport has no negative origin, so the group shifts it down by 960.
     Fill is white because SystemUI tints a tile icon itself. -->
